  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jonah Heim kept them breathing with six RBIs, but Miami's early grip never loosened.",
    "what_this_means": "Heim drove in six runs. More than enough offense in most games. Yet the damage was done before the eighth inning arrived. Miami scored six in the first three innings, and a blowout by the fifth meant this wasn't a game the A's clawed back into. It was a game they lost early and refused to quit from. Zack Gelof started a three-run ninth that made the final score respectable, but respectability isn't a win. This is what inconsistency looks like: the same lineup that can't string anything together produces a six-RBI night and still leaves the field down a run. Heim's power was real. The result wasn't enough.",
    "what_to_watch": "Tarik Skubal threw 3.15 ERA ball last season and Detroit brings that into tomorrow's matchup at 3:40 PM PT. J.T. Ginn has thrown clean baseball his last four starts. 2.73 ERA in that stretch. And that's the matchup worth watching.",
